Pseudo-diff F1 (seam_fp, nothing applied): the hold lands a queued turn's read at the q-quantile of its admission
time, q = lam L / (c + lam L), in place of the fixed 2 s (NTP_HOLD_MARGIN_S, next_turn_prefetch.py:128).
Switch SGLANG_HICACHE_NEXT_TURN_HOLD_QUANTILE (EnvBool False); needs the arrival hold and measured prices (PR1).

What is tracked (PR1's AdmissionErrorTracker, fed in _on_departure where ntp_admit is logged, line 755-770):
  non-readers  err = wait - pred_wait_ql        (both already computed there: stats, plan.pred_wait_ql)
               binned by pred_wait_ql (edges 2, 5, 10, 20 s), last 256 per bin: the error of the estimate of D.
  readers      lag = wait - max(pred_wait_ql, last landing - arrival): what admission adds once both the GPU turn
               and the landing are there (campaign 34: median 0.4 s, q90 2.1 s). Kept apart: a reader's wait
               against pred_wait_ql is the read line (+8 to +27 s median), not an error of D.
  turns with no plan get their prediction at first sight in the queue (self._pred_wait, PR1), so the hold's
  estimate for un-hinted turns is tracked too.
The hold predicts with the same function at a shorter horizon ((position + 0.5) / rate each pass), so it takes the
bin of the wait it predicts now. Checked offline: the error at arrival in a predicted-wait bin and the error at the
first pass the prediction falls to X agree to about 1 s at q10/q90 for X <= 8 s (out_f1_*.txt, parts A and B).

